{
  "id": "perceptual-test",
  "term": "perceptual test",
  "definition": "A perceptual test is a task used to assess how a person interprets sensory information. In this source, it refers specifically to a standard auditory missing-fundamental task used to identify whether a listener is more tuned to the fundamental frequency or to the lower harmonic components of a complex sound.",
